# Boot -> title -> NEW GAME -> vibration prompt -> stage load.
# Usage: ICORECOMP_INPUT_SCRIPT=docs/scripts/newgame.pad
#
# Menu flow (decomp: src/st00a.c func_0020DAC8, src/kanbanBoot.c
# func_001B1800/func_001B19E8/func_001B15F0, src/layout_texture.c
# lt_switch_layout): START on the title screen brings up the boot menu
# (layout 9, 1.5 s fade-in, input locked until the memory card poll
# answers). With no save the menu switches itself to the single-item
# NEW GAME screen (layout 0x0A). CROSS confirms (START also accepted);
# TRIANGLE cancels. The confirm lands only after the fade completes
# (InitStageLight() == 2), so each press below leaves fade margin.
# Confirming NEW GAME opens the vibration ON/OFF prompt (layout 6);
# confirming that starts the game (StageManager mode 2).
#
# Timings verified against the runtime log: the second CROSS triggers the
# title BGM fade plus sceCdStSTART(35925), then the stage stream
# sceCdStINIT/StSTART(lbn=19456) with StREAD bursts, a wave of actor
# threads, and a steady per-frame VU1 render loop.
480 start
490 none
900 cross
910 none
1140 cross
1150 none
